From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jinbu Li <199886831+Jinbu-Li@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:03:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] agent: shared Codex configs use catalogs across homes (#5086)

OpenResearch uses a private CODEX_HOME with a config.toml linked to the
user's main Codex home. The relative Windows catalog name resolved in
that private home, where neither magpie catalog existed, so config/read
failed with JSON-RPC -32603 and os error 2.

Use native absolute paths for new provider and desktop catalog references.
Keep an existing relative reference while its catalog remains selected,
including through Join, for a Windows config also read by WSL (#816).
Disconnect/reconnect adopts the new default on existing connections.
Recognize slash-spelled Windows desktop catalog paths for cleanup too.
Document the shared-home and Windows/WSL compatibility boundaries.

Reported and reproduced by Jinbu-Li in #5086. The preceding commit preserves
Dopetaiga's original #4785 ownCatalog fix; this commit covers both catalogs
and adds the shared-home lifecycle regression.

Verification on the original f44fa2ef6 base, Windows x64 / Go 1.26.8:
- TestCodexCatalogAcrossHomes/provider and /desktop both FAIL before the
  fix: the catalog cannot be read from the private CODEX_HOME. Both PASS
  after it. Seven related top-level tests and their subtests PASS.
- Native/Windows go vet ./..., Linux go vet -tags nogui ./..., native and
  Linux builds, and the Windows nogui build PASS; gofmt and diff checks
  print nothing.
- Real Codex 0.166.0 config/read with the reporter's catalog: relative
  reference reproduces -32603/os error 2; absolute reference succeeds.
  Used identical config bytes in isolated homes; creating a new Windows
  symlink was unavailable. OpenResearch itself was not restarted.
- Full Windows nogui suite: 72 packages PASS, 15 FAIL; gateway reaches
  the 10-minute package timeout. Nine neighboring failures reproduce with
  the original codex.go. This is not a green full-suite claim.
All Go tests use an isolated HOME and fixed Go caches. No live agent
configuration or running gateway was changed. Actual Linux/WSL/macOS and
browser UI tests were not run.

Verification repeated after applying to upstream e928b57f0 plus the #4785
dependency (a6330cb54), on Windows x64 / Go 1.26.8:
- With the parent codex.go selected through go test -overlay, both new
  shared-home subtests FAIL with missing catalog files (real FAIL).
- With this change, eight related top-level tests and their subtests
  PASS in 8.423s:
  go test -tags nogui ./internal/agent -count=1 -v -run
  '^TestCodex(CatalogAcrossHomes|WSLAppAddressKept|DesktopList|NeverNamesGoneCatalog|SyncMendsGoneCatalog|OwnCatalogGoneNotPutBack)'
- go vet ./..., GOOS=linux go vet -tags nogui ./..., Windows native
  go build, Linux nogui build and Windows nogui build all PASS.
- gofmt -l on changed Go files and git diff --check print nothing.
The full suite was not repeated on this newer base; its earlier failures
and the runtime-check limitations above remain disclosed.
